<h1>1. BHD Asia &mdash; Corporate Website</h1>
<p><em>Role of this site: a static, professional reference that gives credibility when pitching high-value corporate clients. Minimal traffic; updated mainly when tailoring to a specific big prospect.</em></p>

<h2>Offerings &amp; Positioning</h2>
<ol>
<li>Can you give the full list of corporate services we should show (e.g. HR consulting, performance management, executive coaching) &mdash; each with a short description?</li>
<li>Which of these do you want to keep promoting, and which do you want to move away from (e.g. generic HR consulting)?</li>
<li>How would you describe BHD Asia's positioning in one line &mdash; premium boutique consultancy, global advisory, etc.?</li>
<li>Are there competitor or reference websites whose tone/look you admire (or want to avoid)?</li>
</ol>

<h2>Brand &amp; Naming</h2>
<ol>
<li>Given the move to global clients, do we keep the name "BHD Asia," or plan a rename? If a rename, do you have any candidate names?</li>
<li>Do we keep the current logo, or refresh it?</li>
<li>How should the legal/tax entities (BHD Asia, Partage Consulting in Japan) be referenced publicly &mdash; shown, or kept behind the scenes?</li>
</ol>

<h2>Credibility Content</h2>
<ol>
<li>Which corporate clients / logos can we display? Any we must NOT name?</li>
<li>Do you have case studies, results, or testimonials from corporate work that we can publish?</li>
<li>What are your key credentials and accreditations to feature (certifications, awards, years of experience)?</li>
</ol>

<h2>Function &amp; Contact</h2>
<ol>
<li>Should the site stay purely informational, or include a contact/enquiry form?</li>
<li>What contact details should appear (email, phone, region, booking link)?</li>
<li>Should BHD Asia link to Humming Being at all, or stay completely separate?</li>
</ol>

<h1>2. Humming Being &mdash; Wellness Website</h1>
<p><em>Role of this site: the active, marketing-driven brand for personal wellness, coaching, and the TR certification. This is where content, social media, and lead conversion happen &mdash; the priority build for 2026.</em></p>

<h2>Brand Identity</h2>
<ol>
<li>Is "Humming Being" the final name? Preferred spelling/spacing (Humming Being vs HummingBeing)?</li>
<li>For the logo &mdash; keep the hummingbird, use the owl, or explore fresh concepts? What symbolism must it carry (resilience, high-frequency vibration)?</li>
<li>What feeling should the brand evoke &mdash; warm/spiritual, calm/premium, energetic? Any colours, fonts, or visual references you love or dislike?</li>
<li>Should the look align with the ODU platform's style for consistency?</li>
</ol>

<h2>Offerings</h2>
<ol>
<li>Please list every wellness offering with name, format (in-person/online), duration, and price: TR Certification, executive/life coaching, retreats, Reiki, shamanic work, etc.</li>
